-- erwartet: M141
-- **Poison 609 -- the RESULT half of the signature, and it is a separate reading.**
--
-- 608 falsifies a parameter; this one falsifies the result, and the two are not the same
-- defect. A parameter mismatch is a machine word at a position that exists on both sides;
-- **here the position does not exist at all** -- `still` promises no result, the slot
-- promises a `u32`, and a caller through the slot reads a register nobody wrote.
--
-- Measured 2026-09-02 against the unchanged checker: **0 errors, 0 hints**, and
-- `100 % coverage` printed underneath. The emitter writes `static void still(uint32_t b);`
-- and `.f = &still`, and `cc -Werror` refuses it: *initialization of
-- `uint32_t (*)(uint32_t)` from incompatible pointer type `void (*)(uint32_t)`*.
-- **C compares the whole signature; the checker had no word for the result at all.**
--
-- **A probe of its own and not a duplicate of 608**: `M141` reaches the result only after
-- every parameter has passed, so a repair that broke the result arm alone would leave 608
-- green. *One probe per reading is what makes a code's coverage claim mean something.*

module gift::a_function_pointer_that_answers_nothing {

static mut STAND : u32 = 0;

type Tafel = {
    f : fn(u32) -> u32
        effects { writes STAND }
        costs   <= 4 ops,
};

impl fn still(b : u32)
    effects { writes STAND }
    costs   <= 3 ops
{
    STAND = b;
}

impl fn baue() -> Tafel
    effects { pure }
    costs   <= 2 ops
{
    return Tafel(f: &still);
}

}
